OL,3,GNEWSAChurch organist has no plans to
OL,4,Astop after 70 years
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn organist who has played the same
OL,7,Fchurch organ for more than 70 years has
OL,8,Fsaid he has no plans to stop.
OL,10,FKeith Watts, 88, plays the reed organ
OL,11,Fat St Thomas a Becket Church in
OL,12,FLydlinch, Dorset, having started piano
OL,13,Flessons at the age of nine before
OL,14,Fmoving on to the organ.
OL,16,FHe is thought to be one of the UK's
OL,17,Flongest-serving church organists,
OL,18,Fhaving played almost continuously since
OL,19,Fhe was 15, with only a few breaks,
OL,20,Fincluding for national service and
OL,21,Frecovery from shoulder operations.
OL,23,APub: 05-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
